The engine source of the Linux speaking library

How the Linux speaking library this plugin ships was built is not recorded:
no command, log or build directory of that build is kept. An engine source of
that time is kept, and this directory holds the three files in which it
differs from the sources the Windows and the macOS libraries were built from.
Every change these three files make, and every change of ../engine_overrides,
was found in the shipped library's own code. That the library was built from
exactly these bytes is not established, and a library cannot show it.

The three are modified copies of files of audio.cpp,
Copyright 2026 ShugoAI LLC, at revision
3174e6b26f11a0e39b4f150961dce98f43ba860d, under the Apache License, Version
2.0, which is this repository's licence too (LICENSE, at its root).

In that kept source the engine is the upstream revision with the five files
of ../engine_overrides, the three files here, and the three files that
scripts/stage_native_path_shim.py derives, each in place of the engine's own.
Compared with the upstream revision file by file (4,524 files, none missing
and none added) it differs in those eleven and in nothing else, but for the
line ends of one script no library is compiled from.

Each file in this directory is listed here with where it comes from and what
was changed.

acoustic_model.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/acoustic_model.cpp
  Upstream sha256: 5cd1e0e79ecbd7a1bea21704946f0237c72fc3c2f021c1c4228024c96c4d46f6
  As kept sha256: 93489ceb29709968a1072b80c94ff994368f384f807045c0fa57cdf59c0b75d2
  Changed: two lines. In AcousticModel::next_stream_step, a stream that
  reaches its frame limit before a natural end is an error, as in the file of
  ../windows_resident/overrides. And a prepared step runtime is reused only
  when its prompt capacity equals the one asked for, where upstream reuses
  one at least as large: that is one of the two changes
  ../capacity-history.patch makes. Nothing else differs.

mimi_decoder.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/mimi_decoder.cpp
  Upstream sha256: d64e4f1b6102d5d3a35f32eed6805ea6a232b055cfca253108e0520723fc5fc4
  As kept sha256: f2745af597e646c7d943d70bfb01abfb8ee272ff450bb1815d2387989bde113e
  Changed: what the file of ../windows_resident/overrides changes (two places
  that configure a streaming transformer block through
  graph_common::pocket_transformer_config, and seventeen lines that mark
  tensors as outputs of the graph), and eleven more lines in three places. It
  includes streaming_tail.h (in the directory above this one), keeps one
  MimiStreamingTailRuntime in the decoder's runtime cache, and, where the
  weights are on a Vulkan backend, runs everything after the decoder's
  transformer through that runtime and returns its result. Nothing else
  differs.

session.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/session.cpp
  Upstream sha256: 2f41f5f323ea24c4ae916dcf08aa97122b4d6fa3e67bb87d4190941e781e5123
  As kept sha256: c678bba50eb5711e0c37512c1e9ff3bdfe92a2ed784d7971dff2e6baeeab0f4d
  Changed: seventeen lines added and seven removed, in three places. Where
  the graph is not planned on the host and the prompt capacity mode is
  Double, the prompt capacity is the canonical capacity for twice the
  request, and is not taken from the controller that remembers the largest
  earlier reply; a request that is not positive, or cannot be doubled, is an
  error ("canonical GPU prompt capacity overflow"). The stream loop's three
  calls are timed and its decoded frames counted through profiling.h (in the
  directory above this one). The other change of ../capacity-history.patch,
  for a graph planned on the host, is NOT in this file. Nothing else
  differs.

"As kept" is the file of that kept source, which is the file here without its
four-line head comment; a test holds the two to that. "Upstream" is the file
of the upstream repository at the revision above.
